---
description: Ebbgate build rules — always follow BUILD_SPEC.md and AGENTS.md
alwaysApply: true
---

- `BUILD_SPEC.md` is the source of truth; `AGENTS.md` lists the conventions below in full. Read both before writing code.
- **One milestone per PR.** Never add a milestone to an open PR: branch `cursor/m<N>-<topic>` from the previous milestone's branch and open a new PR.
- Status: M1 merged. M2 (dispatcher) is PR #1; M3 and M4 are stacked PRs on top of it.
- Invariants (spec §1): a `private` task never goes to the cloud; an unknown tier is `private`; a deferred task is persisted before responding; secrets never appear in logs, errors or responses.
- Every workspace package must resolve from source for typecheck and tests (`ebbgate-source` export condition and vitest alias, as in `packages/core`).
- Reuse existing patterns: `isEntrypoint()` for bins, configurable `host` for listeners, timeouts on every subprocess and HTTP call, conditional SQLite transitions, no silent overwrite of user config.
- Never invent Paperclip API shapes. Check docs.paperclip.ing; otherwise write an interface + fixture in `fixtures/paperclip/` + `TODO(verify-paperclip)`.
- Before finishing, from a clean tree: `rm -rf packages/*/dist && pnpm lint && pnpm typecheck && pnpm test && pnpm build`.
